For every $A,T\ge2$, $Q\in[0,T/4]$ and $B\in[0,T-1]$,
universal constants $c,C>0$ satisfy
\begin{equation}
 c\Xi\le\mathfrak R(A,T;Q,B)
       \le C\log(AT)\,\Xi.
 \label{eq:jointminimax}
\end{equation}
If $Q=0$, the sharper upper bound $C\Xi$ holds without logarithms.

Let $n=A-1$ and $q=T-1$. If $r_0\le gnq/2$, then
\begin{equation}
 r_1\ge\frac{g^2nq}{8(r_0+gn)}.
 \label{eq:tradeoff}
\end{equation}
For every policy, $r_1\ge r_0-g$.
